# Project One Move-Between-Rooms Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: conceptual support for M6; movement design for M7
#
# Review the course-provided movement flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, WHILE, SET, or similar terms.

SET direction to the player's movement direction
SET current_room to the player's current room

OUTPUT "Enter a direction: north, south, east, or west"
INPUT direction 

IF direction is available from current_room
    SET movement_valid to true
ELSE 
    SET movement_valid to false 
END IF         

IF movement_valid is true
    SET current_room to the room in the chosen direction 
    OUTPUT "You move to" + current_room
END IF     

IF movement_valid is false
    OUTPUT "you can't go that way"
    OUTPUT "Available exits are the valid directions from " + current_room 
END IF    
WHILE the game has not ended 
    repeat the movement process
END WHILE 
RETURN current_room     
